      "artist": "Gareth Foster",
      "description": "Rum: Mausoleum. The Bullough mausoleum is on the cliff top at Harris, on the opposite\nside of the island to Kinloch Castle and the usual landing place,\nfortunately the wind was right (rare!) for a landing there.\nThe mausoleum you see today is a greek temple of the early 20th century.\nNearby there was a previous, partly underground and tiled establishment\nwhich, it is said, the owner had blown up after someone likened it to a\npublic lavatory, the tiling is now starting to emerge from the ground\n\nand looks as if it should be excavated.",
